<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">First Auditor Appointment Process</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p><strong>Step 1: Identify Qualified Auditor</strong> - ICAI-registered CA (individual or firm). Not disqualified under Section 141. Cannot provide bookkeeping (Section 144). Patron maintains a Gurugram CA network across fee ranges and industry specialisations.</p><p><strong>Step 2: Obtain Consent + Eligibility</strong> - Written consent letter + eligibility certificate confirming Section 141 compliance. Mandatory prerequisites before Board Resolution.</p><p><strong>Step 3: Board Resolution within 30 Days</strong> - Pass resolution appointing first auditor under Section 139(6). Specify: auditor name, FRN, ICAI membership, fees, term (till first AGM). If Board fails within 30 days, shareholders appoint at EGM within 90 days.</p><p><strong>Step 4: File ADT-1 within 15 Days</strong> - From 14 July 2025, mandatory for first auditor (previously optional). File on MCA V3 with ROC Haryana. Attach: resolution, consent, eligibility certificate.</p><p><strong>Note:</strong> For company incorporation, see <a href="/private-limited-company-registration">Private Limited Registration</a>.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Appointment of Auditor in Gurugram:</strong></p>
                    <p><strong>ADT-1:</strong> Statutory notice filed with ROC to intimate auditor appointment. Contains CIN, auditor details, date, term, fees. Due within 15 days.</p><p><strong>Section 139:</strong> Companies Act provision governing appointment, term, rotation, and casual vacancy of statutory auditors.</p><p><strong>Section 141:</strong> Disqualification grounds - body corporate, employee, business relationship, securities holding, debt, guarantee, fraud conviction, 20-company limit.</p><p><strong>Section 144:</strong> Prohibited services - auditor cannot do bookkeeping, internal audit, financial system design, investment advisory for the same company.</p><p><strong>Rotation:</strong> Individual max 5 years, firm max 10 years (2 terms), then 5-year cooling off for prescribed companies.</p>

                </div>
